  {
    "note": "Recorded live on claude-opus-5-5. example.",
    "input": {
      "turn": 2,
      "text": "Something that lets two apps talk to each other."
    },
    "turn": {
      "sessionId": "ses_demo_api",
      "turn": 3,
      "phase": "example",
      "move": null,
      "level": null,
      "messages": [
        {
          "agent": "app",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "Before API, watch the four moves on a simpler concept: planet."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "First: what kind of thing is a planet? \"A thing\" is too broad, and so is \"something in space\". The closest group is celestial bodies that don't make their own light: opaque celestial bodies."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "What looks like a planet but isn't one? A star shines in the night sky too, but a star makes its own light. A planet only reflects it."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "Something closer: Pluto, a dwarf planet. It orbits the Sun and it's round, so what's missing? It hasn't cleared the other objects out of its path."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "Now, what does something need to count as a planet? It has to orbit a star."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "It needs enough mass for its own gravity to pull it into a round shape."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "And it has cleared its orbit. That's the one Pluto was missing."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "Last: what kinds of planets are there? Rocky ones like Earth and Mars."
        },
        {
          "agent": "example_builder",
          "kind": "example",
          "text": "And giant ones made mostly of gas or ice, like Jupiter and Neptune."
        }
      ],
